<header><p class="enc-kicker">Religion / idea · deity</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sayin</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sayin was the chief god of the ancient Kingdom of Hadramawt in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabia">Arabia</a>, usually understood as a moon god. His main temple stood at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shabwa">Shabwa</a>, the capital, where, according to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pliny-the-elder">Pliny the Elder</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/incense">incense</a> brought in from the producing districts was taxed with a tithe for the god. He was regarded as the patron of the state and its kings.</p></div>
